Z||000003||billyboy||03-07-2001||01:10 AM||||Naturally, a 205 will have a smaller side wall, if that's what you mean by "skinny".  Lets do a quick tire schooling here...  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>Our example tire will be a 205/40/16.  The first number (205) is the width in millimeters.  The second number (40) is the aspect ratio of the tire.  In other words, it is the percentage of how wide the tire is.  In this case, it is 40% as TALL as it is WIDE.  Sooo... if you do the math, 40% of 205mm is 82, so the sidewall is 82mm high.  The last number (16) is the wheel diameter.<P>Now, if the tire was a 215/40/17, theoretically, 40% of 215 is 86, so the side wall would be 86mm high.  Just because tires have the same ASPECT RATIO does not mean that they all have the same side wall height.  If you had a tire from, say, a Plymouth Prowler that is a 335/30/20, it will actually be taller than the 205/40/17, even thought the ASPECT RATIO is smaller.  Reason - 30% of 335 is 100.5mm.  <P>Hope I didn't confuse you too much...  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000004||Tigger||03-07-2001||08:47 AM||||<A HREF="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/tiggerfiero1.jpg" TARGET=_blank>www.fiero.nl/uploads/tiggerfiero1.jpg</A><P>These are 205-40's on a 17x7.5 rim w/45mm offset.  Yes, drive on grass and your sidewall will magically disappear!<P>My Fiero has a slight 4x4 look, but I'm fixing that this spring by dropping it 2"<p>[This message has been edited by Tigger (edited 03-07-2001).]||||reg||1
